<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-Stable Danish crown in coming year - poll.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Stable Danish crown in coming year - poll.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Danish crown is expected to fall slightly but remain basically stable between 3.8158-3.8292 per mark in the next 12 months, according to a Reuter survey issued on Monday.</p>
<p>Thirteen Danish and foreign banks and brokerage firms were asked in recent days to predict where exchange rates would be three, six and 12 months from now. They came up with the following average forecasts.</p>
<p>			    3-mo	6-mo	12-mo</p>
<p>Crowns per mark	 3.8158    3.8200    3.8292</p>
<p>The Danish crown traded at 3.8089 per mark at 0830 GMT on Monday April 14.</p>
<p>Crowns per mark:</p>
<p>					  3-mths   6-mths   12-mths</p>
<p>Den Danske Bank		     3.81     -	3.81</p>
<p>Unibank				 3.81    3.81    3.81</p>
<p>Jyske Bank			    3.81    3.81    3.81</p>
<p>Spar Nord			     3.81    3.82    3.83</p>
<p>Sydbank				 3.81    3.81    3.83</p>
<p>Codan Bank			    3.81    3.81    3.81</p>
<p>Midtbank				3.8150  3.8150  3.8150</p>
<p>Citibank				3.80    3.82    3.85</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs			 3.82    3.82    3.84</p>
<p>LB Kiel				 3.81    3.81    3.81</p>
<p>BZW				     3.86    3.85    3.90</p>
<p>Lehman Bros			   3.83    3.84    3.84</p>
<p>Anonymous			     3.81    3.250   3.8250</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
